  "slug": "inference-fit-6a61",
  "summary": "Six November 2026 preprints target inference cost and robustness for GW, Euclid, LSST and SKA analyses, from posterior reuse to a 16-team EoR comparison.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is inference infrastructure for next-generation cosmological datasets. ASPIRE reuses existing posteriors for joint dark-siren cosmological and population inference, with 6-28x speedups over reanalysis. samsara++ implements trans-dimensional MCMC in C++/CUDA for LISA global fits with overlapping Galactic binaries and noise. The LSST DESC cluster pipeline is validated on cosmoDC2 mocks, constraining Omega_c and sigma_8 from cluster counts. On the machine-learning side, Euclid DR1 strong-lens detection depends strongly on training-set composition, image format and ensembling, and EuclidFM learns 128-dim embeddings from Q1 photometry. SKA SDC3b compares 16 teams' EoR pipelines and finds inter-team variability, which highlights methodological systematics. The items are heterogeneous in probe but share a focus on computational efficiency and validation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
